      <h2 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal leading-[1.15] mb-8" style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);">
        Does insurance cover doula costs?
      </h2>

      <img src="/images/hands-on-belly.webp" alt="Hands resting on a pregnant belly, representing care and support during pregnancy" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] object-cover rounded-xl shadow-md mb-8" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" />

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="border-b border-tjb-lavender-300/40 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg mb-2">Private insurance</h3>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed">Some insurers are beginning to cover doula services as part of maternal wellness benefits. This is especially true for employer-sponsored plans through companies prioritizing maternal health outcomes. For example, <a href="https://www.uhc.com/health-and-wellness/health-topics/pregnancy/doula" class="text-tjb-rose-500 hover:underline" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">UnitedHealthcare's doula coverage guide</a> outlines what their plans may include. Ask your plan directly, don't assume the answer is no. To see how coverage varies across insurers and states, the <a href="https://healthlaw.org/private-insurance-coverage-of-doula-care-spring-2024-state-of-the-states/" class="text-tjb-rose-500 hover:underline" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">National Health Law Program's state-by-state doula coverage tracker</a> is the most comprehensive independent resource.</p>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed mt-3">In practice, coverage outcomes can vary even within the same insurance company. Some families have successfully requested in-network exceptions from their insurance provider for doula care, though results vary by insurer and even by which representative you speak to. We've heard from mothers who got approved by one representative and denied by another at the same insurance company. If you get a no the first time, it's worth calling back, asking for a supervisor, and referencing your plan's maternal health benefits specifically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-b border-tjb-lavender-300/40 pb-6">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg mb-2">Medicaid</h3>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed">Medicaid doula coverage is expanding state by state. As of 2026, several states including Texas are moving toward reimbursing doula services. Check with your Medicaid managed care plan for current benefits, or see our <a href="/medicaid-doula-coverage/" class="text-tjb-rose-500 hover:underline">state-by-state Medicaid doula coverage guide</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg mb-2">FSA / HSA</h3>
