            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">Some private insurers are starting to cover doula services, particularly as part of maternal wellness benefits. Medicaid coverage for doulas is also expanding in many states. In practice, results vary widely. We've seen families successfully request in-network exceptions from their insurance provider for doula care, though outcomes can depend on which representative you speak to. If the first answer is no, call back and ask again. You'll need to check directly with your plan.</p>
