            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">Research shows that doula support leads to 39% fewer C-sections, shorter labors, and higher satisfaction with the birth experience. For many families, the cost is justified by improved outcomes and reduced need for medical interventions, which can carry their own costs.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="group pb-3">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer py-2 list-none">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-tjb-charcoal text-lg">How much does it cost to hire a doula?</h3>
            <span class="text-tjb-rose-500 text-xl transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-tjb-gray leading-relaxed pb-2">Hiring a birth doula typically costs $650 to $3,000 for a full package. Hiring a postpartum doula costs $25 to $50 per hour. Some doulas offer sliding-scale fees, payment plans, or reduced rates for students completing their certification.</p>
        </details>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

